t", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01K1V3CoVTZ4WeuKooJgZnW8", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 90662, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01ST7fGDwPWi38pdbiZRtQa7", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled checkout-api back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback was approved and verified. After the rollback, the service reports healthy in all regions on v2.3.0, with an error rate of 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 91262, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01ST7fGDwPWi38pdbiZRtQa7", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 91262, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01ST7fGDwPWi38pdbiZRtQa7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 95659, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **What went wrong:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback needed approval, which was granted, and the system verified it.\n- **Current status:** All three regions now run v2.3.0, report healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback and the current status. It also notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's redeployed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UYHFEppumjbz3m8FMubdg4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TQiKjU9sUkmpvngJvf5QhY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XnfBjhkAWLTNxNn5D7F4cw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011xPDJuao7KRwZvXnWFDYTf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01K1V3CoVTZ4WeuKooJgZnW8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ST7fGDwPWi38pdbiZRtQa7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled checkout-api back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback was approved and verified. After the rollback, the service reports healthy in all regions on v2.3.0, with an error rate of 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **What went wrong:** All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1, which was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback needed approval, which was granted, and the system verified it.\n- **Current status:** All three regions now run v2.3.0, report healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback and the current status. It also notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's redeployed.", "type": "text"}]}]}